From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UniXNU-piano <noreply@unixnu-piano.invalid>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:15:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] k27: piano-llcc-island-live=1 (the LLCC island read at each
 ss3 decision) and piano-sleep-cancel=1 (a driver's cancel of the suspend in
 progress)

Two follow-ups of 0061/0062 (UniXNU-piano docs/power.md §3.6, §7), each off unless its argument is set:

- piano-llcc-island-live=1: 0061 read the LLCC ISLAND1 words (TRP_ATTR0 0x26841300, ATTR1 0x26841308, through the broadcast
  base) once at boot, before any kext, so a slice PianoA830 programs later (piano-llcc-island=1) stayed "NOT reserved" and ss3
  needed piano-llcc-island-ok=1. Live, ss3 is decided on the two words read at that decision: the idle loop reads them only when
  every other condition of ss3 already holds (the last CPU of all, its deadline, the latency holds; piano_pm_pick_domain_island),
  a suspend reads them at its entry for its level (and logs the reading). Read only, the boot reading's two loads through the
  window it mapped. piano-cpuidle=3 is no longer refused at boot in this mode (ss3 waits for the slice); the cpuidle summary and
  each suspend's entry say when the verdict changes; machdep.piano_cpuidle / piano_sleep show the live reads.
- piano-sleep-cancel=1: a driver that cannot take part in this sleep asks piano_s2idle_cancel(who, why), or IOPMrootDomain's
  callPlatformFunction("piano-sleep-cancel", who, why) without linking this kernel (an older kernel answers Unsupported), during
  its kOff or its PreSleep platform action. The window opens at willNotifyPowerChildren (the sleep state), is opened again
  (keeping what was asked) when IOCPUSleepKernel starts, and shuts at the freeze. Cancelled, the suspend returns before the
  park, or abandons the park the way a CPU that does not park does: nothing is suspended, PostResume runs, a normal full wake
  with the reason "piano.cancelled". The first caller's name and reason are logged and kept; refusals (argument off, no sleep in
  progress, too late) are logged (the first 16, then every 64th) and the sleep goes on as before.
  piano-sleep-cancel-test=N: the kernel's own test caller asks, through IOPMrootDomain's function, at PreSleep of suspend N.
- The decisions are osfmk/arm64/piano_s2idle_policy.h = UniXNU-piano tooling/k27/piano-pm/piano_s2idle_policy.h (host-tested).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
